# Trading Dashboard

The dashboard is an observability and control interface.

It is NOT a source of trading authority.

---

## Architecture

One central React application.

Sports are pages/views:

/mlb
/nba
/ncaab
/nfl

Shared components should be reused.

---

## Dashboard Must Show

System:
- environment
- trading mode
- connection state
- last market-data timestamp
- reconciliation state
- kill switch

Positions:
- open positions
- quantity
- average entry
- current market
- unrealized P&L
- realized P&L
- exit state

Orders:
- working
- filled
- partially filled
- cancelled
- rejected
- unknown

Risk:
- bankroll
- exposure
- limits
- remaining capacity
- daily trade count
- daily P&L

---

## Safety

UI controls that can affect trading must require explicit confirmation.

Never make destructive trading actions one-click without confirmation.

Dashboard must clearly distinguish:

PAPER

from:

LIVE
